    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self-Attested RC Photocopy:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The original Registration Certificate (RC) must remain with the vehicle owner. Provide a clear, self-attested photocopy to the transporter. This document verifies ownership and is required for interstate movement. Ensure the name on the RC matches the ID proof provided.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is mandatory for all registered vehicles. Although the vehicle may be transported on a carrier, the PUC must be within validity to avoid legal complications during transit checkpoints.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Your existing comprehensive or third-party insurance policy must be active. Transporters will verify this before loading. This covers liability in case of an accident involving the carrier vehicle, not the transit damage to your car itself.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA-Approved Consignment Bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This is the most critical document for your protection. The IBA (Indian Brokerage Association) approved bilty acts as the contract between you and the transporter. It details the vehicle’s condition, pickup and drop locations, and the agreed transit time. Never dispatch a car without a signed, IBA-compliant bilty.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>While the documents above are standard, the true safeguard for your investment is <strong>100% declared-value marine transit insurance</strong>. Standard transport policies often limit liability to a fraction of the vehicle's market value.</p>
<p>By opting for full declared-value coverage, you ensure that if any damage occurs during transit, the insurance company compensates you for the entire declared value, minus any applicable deductible. This coverage is non-negotiable for high-value cars and is highly recommended for all vehicles to eliminate financial risk.</p>

<p>Before the pickup, conduct a joint inspection with the transporter’s representative. Document pre-existing scratches or dents in the bilty with photographs. This prevents disputes during delivery. Keep all original documents, including your ID proof and address proof, handy in case of checkpoint verification.</p>
<p>With the right paperwork and comprehensive insurance, your affordable car transportation from Ranchi becomes a stress-free, secure, and efficient process. Always verify the transporter’s IBA license number and insurance certificate authenticity before finalizing the booking. Proper documentation is the cornerstone of reliable vehicle logistics, ensuring your car arrives safely and on time.</p></div>
